From u118cea91a1619106 at groups.google.com  Thu Sep 21 10:44:11 2023
From: u118cea91a1619106 at groups.google.com (Murray Efford)
Date: Thu, 21 Sep 2023 10:44:11 +0000
Subject: Re: How to specify occasion per session
Message-ID: <2_LelIrAC0E.hdDFVw9_AQAJ@secrgroup.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/secrgroup/c/2_LelIrAC0E/m/hdDFVw9_AQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

By default make.capthist() and read.capthist() assume that the final occasion (and hence the number of occasions) is the largest occasion in your capture dataset. However, both functions have argument 'noccasions' that may be used to specify the number of occasions, with exactly your situation in mind. For multi-session data the noccasions argument can be a vector with one number per session.

